/-!
# ArithS.Necessitation.Top — the top (`DESIGN_fragments.md` §7) against an explicit kit

The final assembly of U10: from a `TAct`-proof code `ρ` of the `k`-instance `instB ⌜χ⌝ k` with
`dlen ρ ≤ gBudget k`, a proof code of the `k`-instance of the box `Box_g χ` — i.e. of the sentence
"`instB ⌜χ⌝ k` has a proof of length `≤ g(k)`" — of length `≤ C_χ · ((gBudget k)^3 + 1)`, hence
`BoundedInnerNec 3` (`Assembly/Prep.lean` §6). The verification recursion (`Verify.lean`) still lacks
its prologue producers, so its two theorems (§6.3 `verifySteps_ok`, §6.4 `dlen_verifySteps_le`) do
not exist yet; this file states EXACTLY what the top needs from them as the fields of a `Prop`
structure `VerifyKit`, states the per-`χ` pinning of §7.2 as a second structure `PinKit`, and proves
everything else. `boundedInnerNec_three_of_kit` is the top; discharging the two kits is the
remaining `Verify`/`Cert` work (their docstrings say precisely what).

**Universe.** `V : Type` throughout — `BoundedInnerNec` quantifies over `V : Type`, and several
`InstV` lemmas are stated there. TRAP (found here): a statement like `IsSemiterm LAct 0 (qNum χ)`
with `variable {V : Type}` elaborates the `0` BEFORE `V` is pinned and defaults the whole statement
to `V := ℕ` — which type-checks (ℕ is a model) and is USELESS. Every statement ascribes `V`.

## Contents

* §1 The two new predicate codes (`lenDerivableDef TAct`, `boxCore` through the Σ₁ symbol
  `boxCoreS`/`boxRel`), the three new library rows `gIntroNum`, `lenDerIntro`, `boxIntro` (`Lib`,
  soundness by `pa_proves_of_models`), their pieces/`inst_` lemmas, the table
  `topRows := frag2Rows ++ [dlenDefIntro, proofIntro, gIntroNum, lenDerIntro, boxIntro]` at
  `150 + k` (`TopTable`, `exists_topTable`), the pieces `topPieces`, the step lemmas `tok_<row>`
  and `tfok_leTrans` (GENERATED by the session script `gen_top.py` on the `gen_frag2.py` template).
  Design choice (vs. `DESIGN_fragments.md` §7.1 step 9): the target is closed by ONE Horn row
  `boxIntro “n k g a. gGraph a k → instBGraph g n k → lenDerivableDef a g → boxCore n k”`
  whose conclusion IS the target fact, so the leaf is `axLFactCode` — no `targetLeafCode`.
  Likewise `lenDerIntro` folds `proof`/`dlenDef`/`≤` into `lenDerivableDef`, and `gIntroNum`
  reads the cube from the two numeral products directly (no eigenvariable `l̂`, no congruence glue).
* §2 The target's code shape: `instB ⌜Box_g χ⌝ k = boxFact (qNum χ) (bnum k)` with
  `qNum χ := numeral ⌜χ⌝` the unary numeral of the code of `χ` — proved for a VARIABLE `χ`
  (`quote_Box_g`, `instB_quote_Box_g`, `target_eq_boxFact`); the numeral's closedness, shift law and
  length (`termLen (numeral x) ≤ 2x + 1`).
* §3 The root layout `RootLayout` (what the walk + chain of the root sequent `{x}` deliver), the kits
  `VerifyKit` (§6.3/§6.4/§5 for the RELATION `VerifyGraph`) and `PinKit χ` (§7.1 steps 1–4 / §7.2).
* §4 `rootSteps` — the root layout is produced (`describeF` + `chainSteps` + `dossierAt_of_walk`).
* §5 `closeSteps` — from the recovered root goal to the target fact: the four `sLemma` numeral steps
  (N5, N4 ×2, N2) and the five rows.
* §6 The whole list, `chainCode_proof`, and the cost polynomial.
* §7 `boundedInnerNec_three_of_kit : … → BoundedInnerNec 3`.
-/

